    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.listening_items, $seed${"slug":"b1-roommates-sharing-chores","title":"Sharing the Housework","level":"B1","status":"published","sort_order":200,"metadata":{"format":"dialogue","script_type":"dialogue","speakers":["Malika","Sophie"]},"summary":"Two flatmates studying abroad talk politely about a messy kitchen and agree on a cleaning rota.","transcript_text":"Malika: Sophie, have you got a minute? I wanted to talk about the flat.\nSophie: Sure. Is everything OK?\nMalika: Mostly, yes. It's just that the kitchen's been really messy lately, and I feel like I'm always the one cleaning it.\nSophie: Oh, sorry. I didn't realise. I've had so many deadlines this month.\nMalika: I know, me too. So I was thinking, maybe we could make a rota, you know, a list of who does what each week?\nSophie: That's a good idea. What jobs are we talking about?\nMalika: Washing up, taking out the rubbish, cleaning the bathroom and vacuuming.\nSophie: OK. Honestly, I hate cleaning the bathroom. Could I do the washing up every day instead?\nMalika: Every day? That's quite a lot.\nSophie: It's fine, really. I cook most evenings anyway, so it makes sense for me to wash up.\nMalika: All right, then I'll do the bathroom, and we can take turns with the rubbish and the vacuuming, one week each.\nSophie: Deal. Shall we put the rota on the fridge so we don't forget?\nMalika: Perfect. I'll make it tonight.","category":"Daily Life","accent":"general","speed_label":"natural","speed_wpm":140,"duration_seconds":74,"audio_url":null,"focus_skill":"inference","tags":["flatmates","housework","study abroad","dialogue"],"questions":[{"id":"q1","type":"mcq","prompt":"Why does Malika want to talk to Sophie?","options":["Sophie is too noisy at night.","She feels she always cleans the messy kitchen.","She wants to move out.","The rent is going up."],"answer_index":1,"explanation":"\"The kitchen's been really messy lately, and I feel like I'm always the one cleaning it.\""},{"id":"q2","type":"mcq","prompt":"How does Sophie react at first?","options":["She gets angry.","She says it isn't her fault.","She apologises and explains she has been busy.","She ignores the problem."],"answer_index":2,"explanation":"\"Oh, sorry. I didn't realise. I've had so many deadlines this month.\""},{"id":"q3","type":"mcq","prompt":"Why does Sophie offer to wash up every day?","options":["She cooks most evenings anyway.","She likes washing up.","Malika asks her to.","She has a dishwasher."],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"\"I cook most evenings anyway, so it makes sense.\" She also says she hates cleaning the bathroom."},{"id":"q4","type":"mcq","prompt":"What do they decide about the rubbish and the vacuuming?","options":["Malika will do both.","Sophie will do both.","They will pay a cleaner.","They will take turns, one week each."],"answer_index":3,"explanation":"\"We can take turns with the rubbish and the vacuuming, one week each.\""}]}$seed$::jsonb) r
