    select r.slug, r.title, r.level, r.status, r.sort_order, r.metadata, r.summary, r.transcript_text, r.category, r.accent, r.speed_label, r.speed_wpm, r.duration_seconds, r.audio_url, r.focus_skill, r.tags, r.questions, v_product_listening, v_en_id
    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.listening_items, $seed${"slug":"c1-seminar-is-online-learning-as-good","title":"Seminar: Is Online Learning as Good?","level":"C1","status":"published","sort_order":200,"metadata":{"format":"dialogue","script_type":"dialogue","speakers":["Madina","Tom"]},"summary":"Two students debate in a university seminar whether online courses can match learning on campus, and find more common ground than they expected.","transcript_text":"Madina: I'll start, if that's okay. I'd argue that online learning can be just as effective as studying on campus, provided it's designed properly.\nTom: Provided being the key word there, isn't it? Most of the online courses I've taken were basically recorded lectures with a quiz at the end.\nMadina: Fair point, but that's an argument against bad course design, not against online learning itself. A dull lecture in a hall isn't any better just because you're physically there.\nTom: I'm not so sure. Being in the same room creates a kind of pressure that I think is actually useful. You can't just switch off your camera and wander off to make tea.\nMadina: True, though for a lot of people that flexibility is the whole point. Think about someone working full-time in Namangan who wants a degree from a university in Tashkent, or abroad. For them, online study isn't a weaker version of campus life. It's the only version available.\nTom: Okay, I accept that, and access is a genuinely strong argument. My concern is more about what gets lost: the conversations in the corridor, the chance meetings that turn into projects.\nMadina: Some of that can be built in, with small group work and live discussions. But I'll admit it doesn't happen naturally. Someone has to make it happen.\nTom: So perhaps we actually agree more than it seemed. The real question isn't online versus on campus. It's whether a course is designed around people actually talking to each other.\nMadina: I think that's a fair summary, yes.","category":"Work and Study","accent":"general","speed_label":"natural","speed_wpm":160,"duration_seconds":95,"audio_url":null,"focus_skill":"inference","tags":["education","debate","online learning","dialogue"],"questions":[{"id":"q1","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is Madina's position at the start of the discussion?","options":["Online learning is always better than campus study.","Campus study is necessary for a real degree.","Online learning can work as well as campus study if it is well designed.","Lectures should be replaced by quizzes."],"answer_index":2,"explanation":"\"Online learning can be just as effective as studying on campus, provided it's designed properly.\""},{"id":"q2","type":"mcq","prompt":"Why does Tom mention recorded lectures with a quiz?","options":["To give an example of the weak online courses he has experienced","To recommend a format he enjoyed","To show that quizzes are the best test","To explain why he prefers studying alone"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"\"Most of the online courses I've taken were basically recorded lectures with a quiz at the end.\""},{"id":"q3","type":"mcq","prompt":"What advantage of being in the same room does Tom point out?","options":["It is cheaper for students.","Lectures are shorter.","Teachers give better marks.","It creates a useful pressure to stay focused."],"answer_index":3,"explanation":"\"Being in the same room creates a kind of pressure that I think is actually useful.\""},{"id":"q4","type":"mcq","prompt":"Why does Madina mention someone working full-time in Namangan?","options":["To complain about travel in Uzbekistan","To show that for some people online study is the only option","To argue that working students learn faster","To describe her own situation"],"answer_index":1,"explanation":"\"For them, online study isn't a weaker version of campus life. It's the only version available.\""},{"id":"q5","type":"mcq","prompt":"How does the discussion end?","options":["Tom changes his mind completely.","They agree to disagree.","They agree that course design, and real interaction, matters most.","Madina admits that campus study is better."],"answer_index":2,"explanation":"Tom: \"So perhaps we actually agree more than it seemed.\" Madina: \"I think that's a fair summary.\""}]}$seed$::jsonb) r
