    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.immersion_missions, $seed${"slug":"c1-negotiating-a-lease-renewal","title":"Negotiating a lease renewal","level":"C1","status":"published","sort_order":200,"metadata":{},"context_text":"You have rented a one-bedroom flat in Istanbul for two years while working for a software company. You have always paid on time and looked after the flat. Your landlord has just sent a notice proposing a significant rent increase for the next year, and you would like to stay, but not at that price.","objective_text":"Understand the notice and your options, learn the landlord's real position, write a reasoned counter-offer, and negotiate a compromise on the phone.","mission_type":"problem_solving","target_vocabulary":["lease","renewal","rent increase","notice period","counter-offer","fixed term","reliable tenant"],"target_grammar":"conditionals and concessions for negotiation (If you were willing to…, I'd be prepared to…; While I understand…, …)","cultural_note":"Landlords often value a reliable long-term tenant more than a slightly higher rent, because an empty flat and a new tenant both cost money. Framing your offer around reliability and commitment is usually more persuasive than simply saying the increase is unfair. Tenancy rules differ by country, so check the local regulations before you negotiate.","success_conditions_json":["Identify the proposed terms and the response deadline","Understand the landlord's underlying motivation","Write a polite, reasoned counter-offer","Negotiate on the phone and agree clear terms"],"skill_mix":["reading","listening","writing","speaking"]}$seed$::jsonb) r
