    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.immersion_mission_steps, $seed${"step_index":3,"service_key":"speaking","step_type":"speak","title":"Rein in the dominating speaker","instructions":"Twenty minutes into the discussion, Mr Laine has been talking for three minutes and has started describing his product's features. Interrupt gracefully, acknowledge his point, redirect the conversation away from the pitch, and bring in Dr Haydarova with a specific question.","prompt_text":"Mr Laine: ...and the new version also includes adaptive quizzes, a parent dashboard, voice support in twelve languages, and we're about to launch a...","expected_answer_json":{"goal":"Interrupt diplomatically, steer away from the pitch and rebalance the panel.","points":[{"label":"interrupt politely","any":["if i could","let me stop you","can i just","sorry to interrupt","i'm going to jump in","conscious of time","pause you there"]},{"label":"acknowledge his point","any":["access","you've made","your point","thank you","clearly","reach","fair"]},{"label":"steer away from product detail","any":["rather than","not about","bigger question","step back","beyond","features","product","specific tool"]},{"label":"bring in the researcher with a question","any":["dr haydarova","haydarova","bring in","evidence","research","what does","does the evidence"]}],"model_answer":"If I could just pause you there, Mr Laine, because I'm conscious of time. You've made the access argument very clearly: students who can't afford a private tutor could suddenly have one. Let's step back from any particular product, though, and test that claim. Dr Haydarova, you've warned that most of the evidence comes from well-resourced schools. Does the research tell us anything yet about the students Mr Laine is describing?"},"target_skill_key":"speaking.task_completion","estimated_minutes":4,"status":"published","metadata":{}}$seed$::jsonb) r;
